WEBVTT

00:01:59.076 --> 00:02:01.316
And the answer came to me
with a sudden clarity.

00:02:01.316 --> 00:02:02.596
It was like, of course,

00:02:02.636 --> 00:02:04.236
he was the writing life

00:02:04.236 --> 00:02:07.196
that I had longed for
since I was four years old.

00:02:07.196 --> 00:02:10.636
He was an emissary
from the beautiful world.

00:02:10.676 --> 00:02:13.156
And just like that,
the obsession fell away,

00:02:13.156 --> 00:02:15.156
and I started writing for real.

00:02:17.116 --> 00:02:20.996
Today, I want to talk with you
about a state of mind

00:02:21.036 --> 00:02:23.636
that's ancient and universal

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.876
and enormously powerful

00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.796
and, strangely, these days overlooked.

00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:31.396
The author C.S. Lewis
called this state of mind